column278:
19/Apr/16 7:29 AM;ochaloup;Hi [~dmichael],

thank you for your changes. I like it. Especially the start of the section on 1PC. But I have a particular objection.

The second paragraph seems to me confusing and misguiding

{code}
The single-phase resource is processed last in the prepare phase of the transaction, and an attempt is made to commit it. If the commit succeeds, the transaction log is written and the remaining resources go through the XA resource. If the last resource fails to commit, the transaction is rolled back. One situation where this might happen is when a non-XA aware datasource needs to participate in the transaction.
{code}

It still mixes the information about 1PC and LRCO.Instead of the mentioned paragraph put following info on 1PC
 * 1PC means that prepare phase (which normally causes creation of lock in the resource till second phase is processed) is skipped and only commit is proceed on the resource
 * if it's not said otherwise 1PC optimization is used automatically when global transaction contains only one participant

After the first paragraph in section LRCO add part of the existing paragraph removed from 1PC section which will be like
{code}
The non-XA resource is processed last in the prepare phase, and an attempt is made to commit it. If the commit succeeds, the transaction log is written and the remaining resources go through the commit phase. If the last resource fails to commit, the transaction is rolled back. 
{code}

