column279:
13/Jan/16 4:40 AM;jmartisk;The example for MUST query doesn't seem correct/useful to me.
{noformat}
//look for popular myths that are preferably urban
Query luceneQuery = mythQB
    .bool()
        .must( queryA )
        .must( queryB )
    .createQuery();
{noformat}

First, I guess the description should say something like 'popular urban myths', but not 'preferably', because 'preferably' describes a SHOULD query.
Second, this example uses just some references to queryA and queryB which are not declared anywhere, it's not clear what they contain. The example should rather build some queries from mythQB, just as the other two examples (SHOULD, MUST NOT) do.

This would work, for example:
{noformat}
//look for popular urban myths
Query luceneQuery = mythQB
    .bool()
      .must( mythQB.keyword().onField("description").matching("urban").createQuery() )
      .must( mythQB.range().onField("starred").above(4).createQuery() )
    .createQuery();
{noformat}

