column282:
15/Nov/10 6:55 PM;awaterma;RESTAPI through existing Guvnor supports the interaction with package contents, and, I (think) the creation of new packages.  The URL:

/org.drools.guvnor.Guvnor/api/packages/

Works for GET, PUT, DELETE and POST for interacting with generic resources in packages on the server.  It seems as though the only functionality that is missing is a call to "compile" for a specific package.  The RESTAPI servlet could be extended to handle the following path:

/org.drools.guvnor.Guvnor/api/compile/package/{packageName}

Although I'm not sure viewing all content from a package perspective is the best.  A rest api where content would be accessible by type, might be nicer.  For example:

/org.drools.guvnor.Guvnor/api/technicalrules/{technicalRuleId}
/org.drools.guvnor.Guvnor/api/models/jars/{jarId}
/org.drools.guvnor.Guvnor/api/packages/{packageId}

An "actions" part of a URL would be useful.  For example:

/org.drools.guvnor.Guvnor/api/packages/{packageName}/compile
/org.drools.guvnor.Guvnor/api/technicalrules/{technicalRuleId}/compile

Actions could be extended (if wanted, or required) to include snapshot creation, test(simulation) execution, etc.

I am attaching, as well, a simple UML diagram for possible resource types as declared in the Guvnor UI.

