column286:
13/Apr/15 7:39 AM;grgrzybek;Good point
I just checked, but it's actually not deprecated, because those options are not for e.g., appending to list of bundles, but to particular pid/config/system property, like:

{noformat}
JBossFuse:karaf@root> profile-edit --config a=b,c=d x
Setting value:b,c=d key:a from config properties and profile:x version:null
{noformat}
this will make config property {{a}} with value {{b,c=d}}, so it's not correct.

{noformat}
JBossFuse:karaf@root> profile-edit --config a=b --config c=d x
Setting value:b key:a from config properties and profile:x version:null
Setting value:d key:c from config properties and profile:x version:null
{noformat}
this will make config property {{a}} with value {{b}} and {{c}} with value {{d}} so it's correct.

{noformat}
JBossFuse:karaf@root> profile-edit --append --config a=xx x
Appending value:xx key:a from config properties and profile:x version:null
{noformat}
this will append {{,xx}} to the value of property {{a}}, so {{a}} will now have value {{b,xx}}.

