See the JCR/Kernel class org.exoplatform.management.jmx.impl.PropertyInfo.java
When a Object has dynamic property value, there are double-quote characters in value
{code}
private class DynamicValue extends Value
{

      String resolve(Object instance)
      {
         ...
         return ObjectName.quote(value.toString());
      }
   }
{code}
This created a bug when jmx client is on Web Browser. See bug effect here: https://issues.jboss.org/browse/GTNPORTAL-362. We can test it in GateIn Jboss + jmx-console.
So I think we should remove this for property value. It should be:
{code}
return value.toString();
{code}

In validation of adding child node we check if primary type is allowed:

{code}
 if (!nodeTypeDataManager.isChildNodePrimaryTypeAllowed(primaryTypeName, nodeData().getPrimaryTypeName(),
         nodeData().getMixinTypeNames()))
      {
         throw new ConstraintViolationException("Can't add node " + sysLocFactory.createJCRName(name).getAsString()
            + " to " + getPath() + " node type " + sysLocFactory.createJCRName(primaryTypeName).getAsString()
            + " is not allowed as child's node type for parent node type ");

      }
{code}

But actually needed also to take in account node name. 
For example, there is node A which allow nodes: with name B1 and node type T1, with name B2 and node type T2. When we are trying to add node B1 with node type T2 the validation will be passed, but should not.

During refactoring JCROrgService two issues about specification were revealed. The first one is about removing group where children groups still exist. Specs says:

{quote}
Use this method to remove a group from the group database. If the group has he children group. The method should not remove the group and throw and exception
{quote}

Current implementations merely removes group and all its children. The second one is about saving user profile for not existed user.
Specs says nothing but more logically to throw an exception than just skip saving.

