column47:
To ensure that the queries are correct the best thing to do is to launch a clean PLF instance then test if the consistency check tool indicates that the JCR is consistent if not I guess it probably means that the queries are not good.

Using this technique, I realized that the following queries should be reviewed by adding the filter P_MULTIVALUED=0 since the spec doesn't forbid it in case of multi-values, I quote "it is possible to have a multi-value property with no values (an empty array)":
{code}
select * from JCR_SITEM P where P.CONTAINER_NAME='workspaceName' and P.I_CLASS=2 and NOT EXISTS( select * from JCR_SVALUE V where V.PROPERTY_ID=P.ID)

select * from JCR_SITEM P where P.CONTAINER_NAME='workspaceName' and P.P_TYPE=9 and NOT EXISTS( select * from JCR_SREF R where P.ID=R.PROPERTY_ID)
{code}

The next query should be removed since we cannot know if they are real violations due to import process that allows adding reference properties that refers to a missing node:
{code}

select * from JCR_SREF R, JCR_SITEM I where R.PROPERTY_ID = I.ID and I.CONTAINER_NAME='workspaceName' and NOT EXISTS(select * from JCR_SITEM N 
    where N.CONTAINER_NAME='workspaceName' and R.NODE_ID=N.ID)
{code}

Moreover the issue https://jira.exoplatform.org/browse/JCR-1711 shows that the following query is not enough:
{code}
select * from JCR_SITEM N where N.CONTAINER_NAME='workspaceName' and N.I_CLASS=1 and NOT EXISTS (select * from JCR_SITEM P where P.I_CLASS=2 and P.PARENT_ID=N.ID and P.CONTAINER_NAME='workspaceName')
{code}
Indeed first of all the filters order doesn't match with the indexes and it should check for the primary type instead, so the query should be something like:
{code}
select * from JCR_SITEM N where N.CONTAINER_NAME='workspaceName' and N.I_CLASS=1 and NOT EXISTS (select * from JCR_SITEM P where P.I_CLASS=2 and P.CONTAINER_NAME='workspaceName' and P.PARENT_ID=N.ID and P.NAME='[http://www.jcp.org/jcr/1.0]primaryType')
{code}

Finally we need also queries to check if all the nodes that have the properties jcr:lockOwner and jcr:lockIsDeep are well defined in the lock tables of type jcrlock_${workspace-name}. The first query will be of type:
{code}
select ID from JCR_SITEM where CONTAINER_NAME='collaboration' and I_CLASS=2 and (NAME='[http://www.jcp.org/jcr/1.0]lockOwner' or NAME='[http://www.jcp.org/jcr/1.0]lockIsDeep')
{code}
If the cache is not shared the second query will be of type:
{code}
select * from jcrlock_collaboration where parent='/$LOCKS'
{code}

If the cache is shared the second query will be of type (to be checked):
{code}
select * from jcrlock_collaboration where parent='${repository-name}_collaboration/$LOCKS'
{code}

column277:
27/Feb/12 5:41 AM;nfilotto;Below, you have the queries for MySQL that allows do identify the nodes that are only defined in one table, it could be nice to check if it could be adapted for all the db type. As it is specific to the LockManager implementation these queries should be launched by the LockManager implementation.


{code:title=What are the nodes only defined as locked in the lock manager tables?}
select * from jcrlock_dms_system where parent='/$LOCKS'
 and fqn NOT IN (select fqn from JCR_SITEM, jcrlock_dms_system where CONTAINER_NAME='dms-system' and I_CLASS=2 and (NAME='[http://www.jcp.org/jcr/1.0]lockOwner' or NAME='[http://www.jcp.org/jcr/1.0]lockIsDeep') and fqn = CONCAT('/$LOCKS/', SUBSTRING(PARENT_ID, CHAR_LENGTH(CONTAINER_NAME) + 1)))
{code}

{code:title=What are the nodes only defined as locked in the jcr tables?}
select PARENT_ID, ID from JCR_SITEM where CONTAINER_NAME='dms-system' and I_CLASS=2 and (NAME='[http://www.jcp.org/jcr/1.0]lockOwner' or NAME='[http://www.jcp.org/jcr/1.0]lockIsDeep') and PARENT_ID NOT IN (select PARENT_ID from JCR_SITEM, jcrlock_dms_system where CONTAINER_NAME='dms-system' and I_CLASS=2 and (NAME='[http://www.jcp.org/jcr/1.0]lockOwner' or NAME='[http://www.jcp.org/jcr/1.0]lockIsDeep') and fqn = CONCAT('/$LOCKS/', SUBSTRING(PARENT_ID, CHAR_LENGTH(CONTAINER_NAME) + 1)))
{code}
Warning : These queries are for JCR 1.12, it must be adapted for JCR 1.14

