25/Apr/12 12:57 PM;nfilotto;Please review each query and rewrite those which are written to use JCR_IDX_SITEM_PARENT_NAME by using filters in the same order as the list of column defined in the index JCR_IDX_SITEM_PARENT_NAME. For example the query:
{code}
select I.NAME, V.DATA, V.ORDER_NUM from JCR_SITEM I, JCR_SVALUE V where I.I_CLASS=2 and I.CONTAINER_NAME=? and I.PARENT_ID=? and (I.NAME='[http://www.jcp.org/jcr/1.0]primaryType' or I.NAME='[http://www.jcp.org/jcr/1.0]mixinTypes' or I.NAME='[http://www.exoplatform.com/jcr/exo/1.0]owner' or I.NAME='[http://www.exoplatform.com/jcr/exo/1.0]permissions') and I.ID=V.PROPERTY_ID
{code}
first check I_CLASS, then CONTAINER_NAME, then the PARENT_ID, then the NAME exactly like the order of the column defined in the index definition which is "I_CLASS, CONTAINER_NAME, PARENT_ID, NAME, I_INDEX, VERSION DESC". The query should be rewritten to match with the order defined in the index JCR_IDX_SITEM_PARENT which is "CONTAINER_NAME, PARENT_ID, NAME, I_INDEX, I_CLASS, VERSION DESC"

