column277:
09/Aug/11 4:05 AM;sergiykarpenko;There are few steps to check DB consistency:

1) Call next queries. If query returns non-empty result - DB is inconsistent.
* Check that all item records has parent item
{code:sql}
select * from JCR_SITEM as I where NOT EXISTS(select * from JCR_SITEM AS P where P.ID = I.PARENT_ID);
{code}
* Check that all nodes have at least one property
{code:sql}
select * from JCR_SITEM as N where N.I_CLASS=1 and NOT EXISTS (select * from JCR_SITEM AS P where P.I_CLASS=2 and P.PARENT_ID=N.ID);
{code}
* Check that all value records has owner-property record
{code:sql}
select * from JCR_SVALUE as V where NOT EXISTS(select * from JCR_SITEM as P where V.PROPERTY_ID = P.ID and P.I_CLASS=2);
{code}
* Check that all properties has at least one value record
{code:sql}
select * from JCR_SITEM as P where P.I_CLASS=2 and NOT EXISTS( select * from JCR_SVALUE as V where V.PROPERTY_ID=P.ID)
{code}
{color:red}Note:{color} Some older jcr versions may support property data without value data. So need to check exact properties without value data.
* Find incorrect JCR_SVALUE records
{code:sql}
select * from JCR_SVALUE where (STORAGE_DESC is null and DATA is null) or (STORAGE_DESC is not null and DATA is not null);
{code}
* Find property records with incorrect property types
{code:sql}
select * from JCR_SITEM where I_CLASS=2 and (P_TYPE=0 or P_TYPE is null);
{code}
* Find reference properties without reference records
{code:sql}
select * from JCR_SITEM AS P where P.P_TYPE=9 and NOT EXISTS( select * from JCR_SREF AS R where P.ID=R.PROPERTY_ID);
{code}
{color:red}Note:{color} Same notation as fro unexisted property values.
* Find reference records that linked to unexisted nodes
{code:sql}
select * from JCR_SREF AS R where NOT EXISTS(select * from JCR_SITEM AS N where R.NODE_ID=N.ID);
{code}

2) Check value storage consistency. At this moment, we can quickly check only amount of stored files and amount of links to files in DB.
{code:sql}
select COUNT(*) from JCR_SVALUE where STORAGE_DESC is not null;
{code}
You can take amount of files on Linux with next command
{code}
find . -type f | wc -l
{code}

There is another option that will check db for sure - reindexation. Reindaxation will itarate all items and index it, so DB structure and content will be checked in best way. Remove index (copy it in safe place) and run jcr - it will start reindexing. Reindex will iterate all items in repository, so exception will be thrown if something is wrong (property not exist or is inconsistent, etc.).
If reindexing finished without exception - JCR Data is consistent.

