16/Aug/11 2:29 AM;sergiykarpenko;There is strange usecase. Some non binary properties, for example primatyType, have binary values stored on file system.

How to find such properties?
{code:sql}
select V.*, P.P_TYPE from JCR_SVALUE as V, JCR_SITEM as P where P.I_CLASS=2 and name='[http://www.jcp.org/jcr/1.0]primaryType' and V.PROPERTY_ID = P.ID and V.DATA is null
{code}
In our case it will return row
{code}
241290, , collaboration608768af0afe1ae0198496cabb87c860, collaboration, 2
{code}
We can find this value stored on file system, using shell script above.
So the value is nt:file.
Then fix the record in JCR_SVALUE table
{code:sql}
update JCR_SVALUE set DATA='[http://www.jcp.org/jcr/nt/1.0]file', STORAGE_DESC=null where (PROPERTY_ID='collaboration608768af0afe1ae0198496cabb87c860') and ORDER_NUM=0;
{code}

