column47:
Originally came from https://jira.exoplatform.org/browse/JCR-1615

There is a mistake when I try to check in a node while its parent node is locked but isDeep = false. A LockException is throwed to notify that the parent node is locked => KO

h4.Investigate:
*1.The context:* 
{code}
parentNode [called A]    //is locked but isDeep = false
    |
    --->node [called B]  //we want to check in this node.
{code}

*2.Analyze code behavior:*

When we {color:red}check in a node{color}, we call *node.checkin()* function. And inside that function, we {color:red}check the parent node{color} is locked or not:
{code}
...
   if (!parent().checkLocking())
         throw new LockException("Node " + parent().getPath() + " is locked ");
...
{code}

Let's go inside this *checkLocking()* function:
{code}
boolean checkLocking() throws RepositoryException
{
   return (session.getLockManager().checkLocking(this.nodeData()) || session.getUserID().equals(SystemIdentity.SYSTEM));
}
{code}
So, if our session is not the system session, then this function will return the result of *checkLocking(nodeData)* function of AbstractSessionLockManager class:
{code}
public boolean checkLocking(NodeData data) throws LockException {
   while (transientManager.isNew(data.getIdentifier())) {
      ...
   }
   return checkPersistedLocks(data);
}
{code}

Now, let's focus on the *checkPersistedLocks(data)* function. we have a problem here:
{code}
protected boolean checkPersistedLocks(NodeData node) throws LockException
{
      LockData lData = null;
      try
      {
         lData = lockManager.getExactNodeOrCloseParentLock(node);
      }
      catch (RepositoryException e)
      {
         throw new LockException(e.getMessage(), e);
      }

      if (lData == null || (!node.getIdentifier().equals(lData.getNodeIdentifier()) && !lData.isDeep()))
      {
         return true;
      }

      // lock exist, so lets check is current session is LockHolder
      return isLockHolder(lData);
}
{code}

Come back to review our context and remember that we are checking "locked" on the parent node(node A) of the node we want to check in (node B). So, the input param of this function is {color:red}the parent node(node A){color}.

First, we get LockData of this node or its ancestor. 
{code}
lData = lockManager.getExactNodeOrCloseParentLock(node);
{code}
=> *lData* contains the locking data of this node or its ancestor. 

Then, we check the *lockdata.isDeep* attribute:
{code}
...
   if (lData == null || (!node.getIdentifier().equals(lData.getNodeIdentifier()) && !lData.isDeep())) {
      return true;
   }
...
{code}
But, because we compare the identifier of the node with one of lockdata: if they {color:red}not equal{color} then we check isDeep value. => if the identifier of node is equal to the one of lData then the isDeep value is not checked => {color:red}NOK{color}

(in our context, the "node" parameter is node A (the parent node) and it's locked => the identifier of node is equal to the identifier of lockdata => the isDeep value is not checked => NOK)

*3.Suggestion:* remove the compare command: {code}!node.getIdentifier().equals(lData.getNodeIdentifier()){code}

Sorry because I wrote so much and made you confused.

GateIn trunk in JBoss-6.0.0.Final with wci-jboss6 JB6ServletContainerContext installed, using the new HttpServletRequest.logout() method, the call to method logout() in: 

org.exoplatform.services.security.j2ee.JbossLoginModule.java  (org.exoplatform.core:exo.core.component.security.core:2.3.7.GA)

produces a warning message:

WARN  [exo.core.component.security.core.JbossLoginModule.class] No principal found when performing JBoss security manager cache eviction for user root

This method should probably check for reentrancy. 

What happens is that the call to HttpServletRequest.logout() from within wci-jboss6 JB6ServletContainerContext triggers a call to:

jbossServer.invoke(securityManagerName, "flushAuthenticationCache", new Object[]{realmName, key},
                     new String[]{String.class.getName(), Principal.class.getName()});

which performs another iteration over LoginModules (causing reentrant call to JbossLoginModule.logout(), which triggers a warning, because cache has already been cleaned on the first call up the stack.


Either WARN should be removed, or reentrancy check should be added, i.e.:

private static final ThreadLocal<Boolean> reentrant = new ThreadLocal<Boolean>();

...

public boolean logout() throws LoginException
{
   if (reentrant.get() != null)
      return true;

   reentrant.set(Boolean.TRUE);
   try
   {
      ...
   }
   finally
   {
      reentrant.remove();
   }
}

