29/Aug/11 10:28 AM;sergiykarpenko;*Research and benchmark results*

*JCR-1579*
Benchmark test SearchNodesByPropertyUsingLikePathOperationTest
runned query
{code}
select * from nt:base where dc:title = 'Exoplatform' and jcr:path like '/" + rootPath + "/%'
{code}

1) clear JCR rev.4794
Index size 170 МБ (178 297 877 байт)  
SearchNodesByPropertyUsingLikePathOperationTest - 5457, 5580, 5755 tps

2) JCR-1579 patch
Unchanged patch
Index size 185 МБ (194 623 095 байт)
SearchNodesByPropertyUsingLikePathOperationTest - 3133, 3053, 2961 tps

3) JCR-1579 + Path NO store
Main idea is to reduce lucene-index size. So make PATH-field unstored.
{code}
doc.add(new Field(FieldNames.PATH, path.toString(), *Field.Store.NO* , Field.Index.NOT_ANALYZED_NO_NORMS));
{code}
Index size 176 МБ (185 062 237 байт)
SearchNodesByPropertyUsingLikePathOperationTest - 3834, 3839, 3842 tps


4) JCR-1579 - get all childs then take Path field
Main idea is to avoid search by stored filed (Field.Store.YES). So we take all child documents by parent id then read PATH and compare

{code}
 TermDocs docs = reader.termDocs(new Term(FieldNames.PARENT, uuid));
 try
 {
    while (docs.next())
    {
       int docId = docs.doc();
       String path = reader.document(docId, FieldSelectors.PATH).get(FieldNames.PATH);
       if (path.equals(nameTest.getAsString()))
       {
          childrenHits.set(docId);
       }
    }
 }
{code}

also path filed size was reduced
{code}
 doc.add(new Field(FieldNames.PATH, *node.getQPath().getName().getAsString()* , Field.Store.YES, Field.Index.NOT_ANALYZED_NO_NORMS));
{code}

Index size 175 МБ (183 971 932 байт)
SearchNodesByPropertyUsingLikePathOperationTest 4167 4221 4307 tps

4) New patch use NAMESPACE_URI and LOCAL_NAME instead PATH
The main idea is to get rid PATH field and use NAMESPACE_URI and LOCAL_NAME fields like in example above.
NAMESPACE_URI and LOCAL_NAME become stored.
