column47:
In issue https://jira.jboss.org/browse/EXOJCR-921
I have found that DefaultItemDataCopyVisitor do not work correct for copying between two workspaces, since there is only one dataManager in constructor (no matter which dataManager you decide, we need two dataManagers - from source workspace and destination workspace).
So, new WorkspaceItemDataCopyVisitor was created.
But it looks a little bit ugly, because ItemDataTraversingVisitor.visit(NodeData nodeData) is overrided just only for use sourceDataManger inside visit(NodeData) and for use destinationDataManager inside DefaultItemDataCopyVisitor logic.

So, the idea is:
- remove  WorkspaceItemDataCopyVisitor;
- add descendantDataManager parameter to DefaultItemDataCopyVisitor (it must be used against dataManager parameter);
- left dataManager as source dataManager to super classes;

What is good:
- code become more understandable;
- no need to external WorkspaceItemDataCopyVisitor;

What is bad:
- if DefaultItemDataCopyVisitor exteders will be used to copy inside one workspace, constructor will contain same data manager for two parameters;

There is usecase which describes problem
 Session sessionWS = (SessionImpl)repository.login(credentials, "ws");
 sessionWS.getRootNode().addNode("myNode", "nt:unstructured");
 sessionWS.save();
 assertTrue(sessionWS.itemExists("/myNode"));
 // copy node to another workspase

 Session sessionWS2 = (SessionImpl)repository.login(credentials, "ws2");
 sessionWS2.getWorkspace().copy("ws", "/myNode", "/myNode"); // exception here

 assertTrue(sessionWS2.itemExists("/myNode"));

