column47:
In the current version, there is noting that prevent us to us a JCR session after a session.logout, so the following code is allowed:

1 Node node = (Node)session.getItem(nodePath) ;
2 session.logout();
3 node.getProperty(propertyName);

At line #3 we expect a RepositoryException which is not the current case. Once the session has been logout, it should possible to access to Session/Item info but it should not be possible to access to data and even more important to modify some data.

To fix this issue, we could add:
      if (!session.isLive())
      {
         throw new RepositoryException("corresponding session has been closed");
      }
to ItemImpl.checkValid() and also create a method checkValid to SessionImpl with the code above as implementation and call checkValid in all the method that access or modify the data

column277:
30/Jun/10 2:35 AM;nfilotto;Very good remark Nikolay, after thinking about it a bit longer, since we need to ensure compatibility between 1.12 and 1.14, we just cannot throw any exception in 1.14, it must be done in 1.15. In 1.14, we will do what you propose i.e., we will use a warning to notify that the operation won't be supported in the next version. So the code should look like:
log.warn("This kind of operation is forbidden after a session.logout(), please note that an exception will be raised in the next jcr version", new Exception());

Could you also create a new JIRA to fix for JCR 1.15 in order to remind us that the warning will be replaced with an exception in 1.15.

