column291:
03/Sep/10 12:58 PM;nfilotto;One last remark is about the fact that TikaDocumentReaderServiceImpl is not really theadsafe anymore since the method getDocumentReader can put and get data concurrently, so you have 2 ways to solve it:
* Make the Map readers_ being a ConcurrentHashMap however it will add a locking overhead that we did not have before
* Make the Map readers_ being a volatile and replace the old code in the cache block with the following code:
{code}
Parser tikaParser = conf.getParser(mimeType = mimeType.toLowerCase());
if (tikaParser != null)
{
   synchronized (this)
   {
      // Check if the reader has been registered since the thread is blocked
      reader = readers_.get(mimeType);
      if (reader != null)
      {
         return reader;	
      }		
      // Initialize the map with the existing values
      Map<String, DocumentReader> tmpReaders = new HashMap<String, DocumentReader>(readers_);
      // Create the TikaDocumentReader for the given mimeType      
      TikaDocumentReader reader = new TikaDocumentReader(tikaParser, mimeType);
      // Register new document reader
      tmpReaders.put(mimeType, reader);
      // Update the map of readers
      this.readers_ = tmpReaders;
      return reader;
   }
}
else
{
   throw new HandlerNotFoundException("No appropriate properties extractor for " + mimeType);
}
{code}
Please note that the second method makes sense because the map will never be big

column277:
02/Sep/10 9:22 AM;areshetnyak;External service for restore into existing workspace should be :
1) Remove existing workspace over repository management;
2) Remove value storage (will get path from WorkspaceEntry);
3) Remove  index folder  (will get path from WorkspaceEntry);
4) Clear old data from DB for this workspace (for single and multi DB that procedure is different);
5) Call restore this workspace.

External service for restore system workspace into existing workspace should be :
1) Remove existing workspace over repository management (will be created special method for remove workspace without checking of system workspace);
2) Remove value storage (will get path from WorkspaceEntry);
3) Remove  index folder  (will get path from WorkspaceEntry);
4) Clear old data from DB for this workspace (for single and multi DB that procedure is different);
5) Call restore this workspace.

If we need restore system workspace, that we should restore other (non system workspace). Because in system workspace was stored version history, node types, etc.

So we need restore system workspace, that we should restore full repository.

So, in this issue, I think we should concentrate on restore full repository in existing repository.

column278:
03/Sep/10 10:24 AM;areshetnyak;External service for restore repository into existing repository should be : 
1) Remove existing repository over repository management (will be created special method for remove repository without checking of default-repository);
2) Remove value storage for all workspaces (will get path from RepositoryEntry);
3) Remove index folder for all workspaces (will get path from RepositoryEntry); 
4) Remove old data from DB (will be implemented in issue EXOJCR-939).
5) Call restore this repository over ManagerBackup.

