Role should be able to create new profile into custom directory, so "default" configuration is preserved.

Ideally the tree structure will look like this:
{{<host-address>/<profile_name>/<configuration_files>}}

Example
{noformat}
10.37.145.210/ha_replication.yaml/<list of broker configs>
10.37.145.210/ha_replication_customized.yaml/<list of broker configs>

10.37.145.211/ha_replication.yaml/<list of broker configs>
10.37.145.211/ha_replication_customized.yaml/<list of broker configs>
{noformat}
This is part of ENTMQBR-2061.

This JIRA talks about reuse of already generated output per VM from provided profiles.
So in case above, call ansible role to *deploy* profile {{ha_replication_customized.yaml/}}

